APPLICATION 1: THE UNIVERSAL CD DIAGNOSTIC
============================================================

  Given ANY comparison system, the CD diagnostic instantly tells you:
  - What algebraic level you're operating at
  - What methods are appropriate
  - What accuracy to expect from simple approaches
  - How much information is structural vs score-determined

  Input: n items, p fraction compared, c confidence
  Output: CD level, effective n, arc accuracy, compression ratio

  System                                              n_eff           CD    Acc   Comp
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────── ────── ──────────── ────── ──────
  Chess Grand Prix (16 players, full round-robin, 100% reliable)   16.0 O (octonion)  57.5%    1.2×
  Premier League (20 teams, 95% games played, 100%)    19.5 S (sedenion)  56.7%    1.1×
  Tennis ATP (100 players, 5% head-to-head, 90% decisive)   18.8 S (sedenion)  56.8%    1.1×
  LLM Benchmark (50 models, 10% compared, 80% agreement)    8.5 H (quaternion)  60.8%    1.3×
  Consumer survey (1000 products, 0.1% compared, 70% consistent)    1.0  R (trivial) 100.0%    1.0×
  Amazon reviews (10K items, 0.01% compared, 60% agree)    1.0  R (trivial) 100.0%    1.0×
  Election (2 candidates, 100% voted, 51% margin)       1.0  R (trivial) 100.0%    1.0×
  Election (5 candidates, ranked choice, 80% respond)    3.3  C (complex)  72.3%    1.8×


APPLICATION 2: LLM BENCHMARK QUALITY ANALYSIS
============================================================

  Modern LLM benchmarks compare models pairwise (e.g., Chatbot Arena).
  The CD ladder tells us when SIMPLE rankings are reliable.

  SCENARIO: Chatbot Arena with 100 models

  5% compared, 70% agreement:
    n_eff = 1.0 → R (trivial)
    Advice: Scores are the complete answer
    Arc accuracy ≈ 100.0%

  5% compared, 90% agreement:
    n_eff = 18.8 → S (sedenion)
    Advice: Algebraic methods fail, need combinatorial
    Arc accuracy ≈ 56.8%

  50% compared, 70% agreement:
    n_eff = 1.0 → R (trivial)
    Advice: Scores are the complete answer
    Arc accuracy ≈ 100.0%

  50% compared, 90% agreement:
    n_eff = 58.4 → Beyond S
    Advice: Pathological regime, no simple theory
    Arc accuracy ≈ 53.7%

  IMPLICATIONS FOR LLM EVALUATION:
  - Most benchmarks are in the QUATERNIONIC regime (n_eff < 9)
    → Simple Elo/Copeland rankings are sufficient
  - Dense benchmarks (>50% compared, >90% agreement) reach OCTONIONIC
    → Need to consider cycle structure, not just win rates
  - Sparse/noisy benchmarks collapse to COMPLEX or even REAL
    → Rankings are essentially arbitrary beyond the top few


